      "actions": [
        {
          "id": "15Iz123NyGFJsKGM",
          "name": "+2 Status to All Saves vs. Arcane",
          "kind": "passive",
          "description": "",
          "traits": []
        },
        {
          "id": "F3wZdkE4SEK62bGg",
          "name": "Best Wishes",
          "kind": "passive",
          "description": "30 feet. Being near a wish dragon gives other creatures a greater sense of what they truly wish for, bolstering their sense of purpose while also distracting them from the task at hand. Creatures in the aura take a –1 status penalty to Perception but gain a +2 status bonus to Will saving throws against mental effects. The wish dragon can't gain the benefit of their own aura or other actions that use the aura, and they can choose to exclude any creatures from any benefit of the aura or action that uses the aura.",
          "traits": [
            "aura",
            "emotion",
            "mental"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "TrsYAH16yYZzQZnp",
          "name": "Wished Away",
          "kind": "reaction",
          "description": "Trigger The dragon is critically hit by an attack\nEffect The dragon wishes not to be hurt by this attack, gaining resistance 25 to all damage against the triggering attack.",
          "traits": []
        },
        {
          "id": "nFPn7CcATGI55G9m",
          "name": "Breath of Loss",
          "kind": "action",
          "description": "The dragon breathes a warm, gentle breeze of mist that creates the feeling of when deepest desires are achieved. As the breeze dissipates, the feeling of loss overwhelms creatures' senses, dealing 19d6 mental damage in a 50-foot type:cone (check (will, dc:41) save). A creature that critically fails its save is also consumed with the memory of the moment and is Stunned 2. The wish dragon can't use Breath of Loss again for 1d4.",
          "traits": [
            "arcane",
            "mental"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "n83M7kH2H3pT9ydc",
          "name": "Destructive Wish",
          "kind": "action",
          "description": "Requirements An illusion from Wish Come True is currently active\nEffect The wish dragon Dismisses the illusion of Wish Come True, which shatters into magical fragments, dealing 9d6 force damage with a check (reflex, dc:41, basic) save to all creatures in a 50-foot type:emanation of the illusion.",
          "traits": []
        },
        {
          "id": "eXPgKMNPkwJjuzFE",
          "name": "Wish Come True",
          "kind": "action",
          "description": "Frequency once per 10 minutes\nEffect The dragon creates an illusion in an unoccupied square within 60 feet that appears to all other creatures that can see it to be the manifestation of their deepest material desire. This has the effects of illusory object (though the illusion might appear to be a creature to certain people) that last for 10 minutes. The wish dragon can Dismiss the illusion. Each non-wish dragon creature who begins their turn within 200 feet in line of sight of the illusion must attempt a check (will, dc:41) save. If any creature within reach of the illusion Interacts to touch it, the illusion ends and that creature is invigorated, gaining 2d8 temporary Hit Points that last for 1 minute.\nCritical Success The creature disbelieves the illusion and becomes temporarily immune to Wish Come True for 1 hour.\nSuccess The creature is unaffected.\nFailure The creature is Stupefied 1 for 1 round.\nCritical Failure The creature is Stupefied 2 for 1 round.",
          "traits": [
            "arcane",
            "auditory",
            "concentrate",
            "emotion",
            "illusion",
            "mental",
            "olfactory",
            "visual"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "4pdrlkii7X9QsUtk",
          "name": "Wish You Would",
          "kind": "action",
          "description": "Requirements An illusion from Wish Come True is active\nEffect The dragon targets one creature within 200 feet currently stupefied by Wish Come True, making them believe that the object of their desires is under attack from all those around them and the dragon is the only one they can trust. The target must succeed at a check (will, dc:40) Save or they become controlled by the dragon for 1 minute. The target may attempt a new save at the end of each of their turns. If the illusion from Wish Come True dissipates, their controlled state immediately ends.",
          "traits": [
            "arcane",
            "concentrate",
            "incapacitation",
            "mental"
          ]
        }
      ],
